The diagram shows the curve $y = f(x)$.
Over which values of $x$ is the curve concave down?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
             xmin=-2.5, xmax=7.4, ymin=-6.7, ymax=6.0, samples=100, clip=false,
             xtick={-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5,6,7}, ytick={-6,-4,-2,2,4}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-1.96:6.62] {0.2*(x*x*x - 6*x*x)};
